  "about": {
    "parts": "The default part binding of separate shells: a trunk that takes the hips, the spine, the chest and the roots of the legs it hides; a neck built apart; a head with its jaw; each leg's shell on its chain and each paw on the bones round the joint it hangs from; a tail.",
    "roll": "The trunk, the neck, the head, the toes and the tail lie along the body, so their Z axis points up; the leg bones stand, so theirs points forward (-Y), as a biped's limbs, and a positive X turn swings a leg forward.",
    "poses": "The review poses: bone-local Euler XYZ rotations in degrees from the rest pose. Each pose exercises one group of joints: a front step, a hind step, a crouch on all four legs, the head turned and lowered, the tail raised. A bone the rig lacks (an optional bone) is left out of a pose.",
    "options": "The sets of optional bones a rig may have: tail, the number of bones of the tail chain from the hips (0: no tail); jaw, 'bone' for a jaw that opens; toes, the toe bones of all four paws, or 'none' for paws rigid on their feet. Every bone not marked optional is required; an optional bone belongs to the rig exactly when an option requires it."
  }
